      dealing: 'Prepare Spanish 40-card or 48-card pack, sometimes with Jokers and deal or lay out cards according to the documented Chinchón rules before play begins.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'Deal seven cards to each player and turn one card to start the discard pile. On each turn a player draws from the stock or discard pile, then discards. A player may close by laying down valid sets and runs when deadwood is low enough; scores are penalties for unmatched card values, with bonuses for gin-like clean hands and special wins for a true chinchón.',
