    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: End a round with the lowest unmatched card value or win immediately with a valid seven-card run.',
      'Turn-flow example: Deal seven cards to each player and turn one card to start the discard pile. On each turn a player draws from the stock or discard pile, then discards. A player may close by laying down valid sets and runs when deadwood is low enough; scores are penalties for unmatched card values, with bonuses for gin-like clean hands and special wins for a true chinchón.',
      'Scoring example: Melds score positive (face value; jokers 0 or as specified); unmelded in hand negative. First to 500 wins. First to 500 points wins. Melds (sets and runs) score positive; unmelded cards in hand count negative. You may take any card from the discard pile but must take all cards above it and meld the drawn card immediately..',
